# Load environment variables in your shell before running the server.
# The default server is local-only. Do not bind it publicly.
# HUB_BIND_HOST=127.0.0.1
# The Dockerfile opts into 0.0.0.0 inside a loopback-published container only.
PORT=4310
HUB_DATA_DIR=./data
# Optional read-only GitHub token. Configure it locally; never commit the value.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
# Optional MCP bearer token. Use a long random value and keep it private.
# HUB_MCP_TOKEN=

# Optional remote HTTPS/OAuth mode: read docs/account-oauth.md first.
# Initialize privately before enabling. Keep the backend port private.
# HUB_PUBLIC_URL=https://zhixu.example.com
# HUB_SESSION_SECRET=
# HUB_TRUST_PROXY=
# Session secret: at least 48 random characters, configured outside Git.
# Proxy trust: exact controlled peer IPs/CIDRs, never true, hop counts, or /0.
# Remove HUB_MCP_TOKEN when enabling remote OAuth.
# Existing VPS updater intentionally rejects extra runtime overrides.
